Package: asus-zenbook-duo-ux8406-second-screen
Architecture: amd64
Depends: udev, ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Description: lower panel of the Zenbook Duo UX8406 off while the keyboard lies on it
 While the detachable keyboard lies on the lower built-in panel, the panel's
 display connector is reported as disconnected, so that the desktop treats it
 like an unplugged monitor and uses its saved layout for the upper panel
 alone. Taking the keyboard off brings the panel back. The lower panel is
 also kept at the brightness of the upper one, which is the only one desktops
 set. udev rules run the helper when the keyboard arrives on or leaves its
 dock port and when the upper panel's brightness changes.
 .
 Does nothing on any other model.

Package: asus-zenbook-duo-ux8406-tcc-guard
Architecture: amd64
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Description: CPU thermal-offset guard for the ASUS Zenbook Duo UX8406
 A service that raises the CPU's thermal offset (the Intel TCC offset) when
 the machine's embedded controller warns of heat, and takes it back once the
 warning is over. Stopping the service restores the original offset. The
 service is enabled and started on installation.
 .
 Logs one line and exits on any other model. An optional configuration file
 is read from /etc/asus-ux8406-tcc-guard.toml; an example is in
 /usr/share/doc/asus-zenbook-duo-ux8406-tcc-guard/.

Package: asus-zenbook-duo-ux8406-keyboard-bpf
Architecture: amd64
Depends: udev-hid-bpf, ${misc:Depends}
Description: HID-BPF program for the hotkeys of the Zenbook Duo UX8406 keyboard
 Makes the function row of the detachable keyboard (USB 0b05:1bf2, Bluetooth
 0b05:1bf3) work with the kernel's generic HID driver: display brightness,
 microphone mute, emoji, MyASUS, the two display keys, the keyboard backlight
 and Fn+Esc. Loaded by udev-hid-bpf when the keyboard connects.

Package: gnome-shell-extension-asus-zenbook-duo-ux8406-keys
Architecture: all
Depends: gnome-shell (>= 45~), ${misc:Depends}
Recommends: asus-zenbook-duo-ux8406-keyboard-bpf
Description: GNOME Shell extension for the display keys of the Zenbook Duo UX8406
 The key right of F12 switches the lower panel on and off, and F8 swaps the
 windows of the two panels. The keyboard delivers these keys with
 asus-zenbook-duo-ux8406-keyboard-bpf.
 .
 To be enabled per user:
 gnome-extensions enable asus-zenbook-duo-ux8406-keys@cceelen.github.io
